{"text": "Te .\nFrom: +\n\nSubject: +\n\n\u00a9 MISSION VIEJO COMPANY\n\nINTER-OFFICE CORRESPONDENCE\n28127 LAPAZROAD + MISSION VEO + CALFORNAS2091\n\nMARIE GALLAGHER Date; MARCH 11, 1996\n\nDANETTE FENSTERMACHER \u201cLeacVE-\n\nPM INSTITUTE--OPERATING AND INTERNAL ACCOUNTING CONTROLS\n\nThe following summarizes my concems surrounding the Institute's control\nenvironment, As you and I have discussed many times in the past, I believe the\ncontrols are very weak in a number of areas of the PM Institute.\n\nDuring a meeting on August 1, 1995, with Dr. Brenner and Kevin Sweeney from\nShook, Hardy & Bacon L-L-P. (S,H&B), I distributed the attached control summary\noutlining the initiation of the implementation of minimum controls for the Institute.\nTo my knowledge the only controls that have been implemented to date are those\n\u2018which my staff and I have established at MVC for the control of the Institute's assets.\nI realize that the Institute has been in a state of flux since the employees originally\ntargeted to start up this venture have not accepted employment with the Institute.\n\u2018S$, H&B has no doubt been kept busy with alternative structures for the organization in\nan effort to attract world renown scientists.\n\n\u2018The fact remains that the Institute and PM in particular, could have potential exposure\nin a number of areas. Listed below is a summary of the issues I believe should be\nimproved by the implementation of intemal controls and operating procedures,\n\n* The lack of supervision for the current employces is a key control missing at the\nInstitute at this time. Without any supervision a whole range of issues are of\nconcem. Some of the more significant areas of concern would be\nappropriateness of the scientific research, disposal of toxic waste, conformance\nto Federal and State safety regulations, and appropriateness of the purchases of\ngoods and services received.\n\n+ The scientists and temporary clerk verbally initiate the purchase of goods and\nservices for the Institute, Payment is made based upon their acknowledgement\nof the receipt of the goods and services. Whether or not the goods and services\n\nza 09 Of3IA NOISSIM Hdb2:rO 96, TT MAM\n\nIDTOTOSbO?",
